msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-info.md:14
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-info.md:16
msgid "Test whether connecting to a remote Nix store via SSH works:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-info.md:18
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix store info --store ssh://mac1\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-info.md:22
msgid "Test whether a URL is a valid binary cache:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-info.md:24
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix store info --store https://cache.nixos.org\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-info.md:28
msgid "Test whether the Nix daemon is up and running:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-info.md:34
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-info.md:36
msgid ""
"This command tests whether a particular Nix store (specified by the argument "
"`--store` _url_) can be accessed. What this means is dependent on the type "
"of the store. For instance, for an SSH store it means that Nix can connect "
"to the specified machine."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-info.md:41
msgid ""
"If the command succeeds, Nix returns a exit code of 0 and does not print any "
"output."
msgstr ""

